# Copy this file to `deploy.config` (gitignored — contains secrets) and
# fill in your HostNext / cPanel details. Then just run: npm run deploy
#
# No SSH needed — deployment runs entirely over cPanel's HTTPS API (UAPI),
# the same port (2083) you use to log into cPanel itself, authenticated
# with your cPanel username + password (HTTP Basic Auth) since "Manage API
# Tokens" isn't available on this hosting plan.
#
# IMPORTANT: this means your actual cPanel login password lives in this
# file. It's gitignored and never committed, but treat it with the same
# care as any other password on disk (don't share this file, consider a
# dedicated/rotatable password if you're worried about reuse elsewhere).
#
# How to find these values:
#
#   CPANEL_HOST — your domain or cPanel account's Shared IP Address
#     (cPanel Home → "Server Information" / "General Information" card).
#
#   CPANEL_USER — your cPanel username (same "General Information" card,
#     labelled "Current User").
#
#   CPANEL_PASSWORD — your actual cPanel login password.
#
#   REPO_PATH — the absolute path to the git repo on the server. Find it in
#     cPanel → "Git Version Control" → your repo → Manage → "Repository
#     Path". (For this project it's the same folder the live app runs from.)
#
#   BRANCH — the git branch that's actually deployed on the server. Check
#     in cPanel → "Git Version Control" → Manage → "Pull or Deploy" tab, or
#     via cPanel Terminal: git -C REPO_PATH branch

CPANEL_HOST=your-domain-or-ip
CPANEL_USER=your-cpanel-username
CPANEL_PASSWORD=your-cpanel-login-password

REPO_PATH=/home/username/your-app-folder

BRANCH=main
